    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and all tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The single test class, `AcceptanceTest`, plus two helper classes make up the suite, and the build also confirms the generated `OwnerDto` now has the `capacityWarning` property (the mapper referencing it compiled).\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a `capacityWarning` flag that is set `true` when an owner's city already holds 40\u201349 owners at create time (approaching the hard limit of 50), mirroring the existing `bulkSignupWarning` pattern. The hard rejection at 50 (`409 CONFLICT`) is unchanged.\n\nChanges:\n\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Added a `CITY_CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 40` constant. Refactored the per-city check to read the count once, reject at `>= 50`, then set `owner.setCapacityWarning(ownersInCity >= 40)` (which can only be true for 40\u201349, since 50+ already returned CONFLICT).\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the `capacityWarning` field (`@Column(name = \"capacity_warning\")`), getter/setter, and a `toString` entry.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added `formatCapacityWarning` (coalescing `null`\u2192`false`), the `@Mapping` for `toOwnerDto`, and the `ignore = true` mapping on the `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` direction (it's a read-only derived field).\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the read-only `capacityWarning` boolean property, which generates `OwnerDto.capacityWarning`.\n- **Schema SQL** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 Added `capacity_warning BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE` so the persisted value round-trips through `getOwner`.\n\nThe acceptance test fills a fresh city to 40 owners, creates the 41st, then `GET`s it and asserts `capacityWarning` is `true` \u2014 which now passes.",
